  "query_id": "Q-1 (R-05)",
  "explanation": "On this hybrid-GPU Windows 11 laptop (Intel Core Ultra 9 275HX iGPU + discrete NVIDIA GeForce RTX 5080 Laptop GPU), all desktop/OS display compositing runs on the Intel iGPU, so the discrete RTX 5080 sits at 0 MiB used when idle. When llama-server loads a GGUF checkpoint with fixed flags, it is the sole CUDA compute process on the RTX 5080 and deterministically allocates the exact same MiB buffer on every load. Profiles captured: ctx=8192 (WO-44 benchmark profile), ctx=32768 (32K production setting), and ctx=65536 (64K reference). Note on small 8K->32K VRAM delta (+172 to +350 MiB): explanation, not measured \u2014 attributed to Gemma 4's hybrid local sliding-window + global GQA attention and q8_0 KV quantization in llama.cpp rather than direct per-layer buffer profiling.",
